C o m p i l a t i o n


      CEE 6410 - Engineering Systems Analysis
      Homework 4 - Reservoir Operation Problem
       
      THE PROBLEM:
       
      A reservoir is designed to provide hydropower and water for irrigation. 
       
      Hydropower and Irrigation Problem Data
      Month   Inflow Units   Hydropower Benefits ($/unit)   Irrigation Benefits ($/unit)
      1       2              1.6                            1.0
      2       2              1.7                            1.2
      3       3              1.8                            1.9
      4       4              1.9                            2.0
      5       3              2.0                            2.2
      6       2              2.0                            2.2
       
      Determine the optimal release amounts between storage, spill, hydropower turbine, diversion to irrigation, and river at point A.
       
      THE SOLUTION:
      Uses General Algebraic Modeling System to Solve this Linear Program
       
      Samuel T. Torgersen-Gonzalez
      s.torgersen-gonzalez@usu.edu
      October 5, 2026
  27   
  28  * 1. DEFINE the SETS
  29  SETS
  30     time months /1*6/;
  31   
  32  * 2. DEFINE input data
  33  PARAMETERS
  34     inflow(time) estimated inflow per month (units)
  35           /1     2
  36            2     2
  37            3     3
  38            4     4
  39            5     3
  40            6     2/
  41   
  42     hydro_ben(time) hydropower benefits per month ($ per unit)
  43           /1     1.6
  44            2     1.7
  45            3     1.8
  46            4     1.9
  47            5     2.0
  48            6     2.0/
  49   
  50     irr_ben(time) irrigation benefits per month ($ per unit)
  51           /1     1.0
  52            2     1.2
  53            3     1.9
  54            4     2.0
  55            5     2.2
  56            6     2.2/;
  57   
  58  SCALARS
  59     stor_i       initial reservoir storage       /5/
  60     stor_max     maximum reservoir capacity      /9/
  61     turb_max     maximum turbine capacity        /4/
  62     min_flow     minimum river flow at point A   /1/;
  63   
  64   
  65  * 3. DEFINE the variables
  66  VARIABLES
  67     storage(time)    reservoir storage at the end of month (units)
  68     hydro(time)      water released through turbines (units)
  69     spill(time)      water spilled to river (units)
  70     irr(time)        water diverted to irrigation (units)
  71     flowA(time)      instream flow at point A (units)
  72     benefit          total economic benefit ($);
  73   
  74  * Non-negativity constraints
  75  POSITIVE VARIABLES storage, hydro, spill, irr, flowA;
  76   
  77  * 4. COMBINE variables and data in equations
  78  EQUATIONS
  79     max_benefit              Objective function to maximize total benefits ($)
  80     mass_balance(time)       Reservoir storage mass balance equation (units)
  81     turbine_capacity(time)   Hydropower turbine capacity limit (units)
  82     storage_capacity(time)   Reservoir maximum storage volume limit (units)
  83     river_flow(time)         Flow continuity downstream of the dam before irrigation (units)
  84     flow_at_A(time)          In-stream flow requirement at point A (units)
  85     ending_storage           Ending storage must be greater than or equal to initial storage (units);
  86   
  87  max_benefit..               benefit =E= SUM(time, hydro_ben(time)*hydro(time) + irr_ben(time)*irr(time));
  88  mass_balance(time)..        storage(time) =E= (stor_i$(ORD(time)=1) + storage(time-1)$(ORD(time)>1)) + inflow(time) - hydro(time) - spill(time);
  89  turbine_capacity(time)..    hydro(time) =L= turb_max;
  90  storage_capacity(time)..    storage(time) =L= stor_max;
  91  river_flow(time)..          flowA(time) + irr(time) =E= hydro(time) + spill(time);
  92  flow_at_A(time)..           flowA(time) =G= min_flow;
  93  ending_storage..            storage('6') =G= stor_i;
  94   
  95  * 5. DEFINE the MODEL from the EQUATIONS
  96  *Can write explicitly
  97  *MODEL SHIPPING /COST, SUPPLY_CONSTRAIN, DEAL_CONSTRAIN/;
  98  *Alternative way to write (include all previously defined equations)
  99  MODEL RESERVOIR /ALL/;
 100   
 101  * 6. SOLVE the MODEL
 102  * Solve the PRODUCTING model using a Linear Programming Solver (see File=>Options=>Solvers)
 103  *     to maximize VPROFIT
 104  SOLVE RESERVOIR USING LP MAXIMIZING BENEFIT;
 105   
 106   
 107  * 7. CLick File menu => RUN (F9) or Solve icon and examine solution report in .LST file


